# Settings architecture (pointer)

Full law: [`docs/docs/architecture/settings.md`](../../docs/docs/architecture/settings.md).

**Permanent decision:** AsteronEngine is multi-project. If a value **can** be a
setting for another game, it **must** be a **Project setting**, **Scene
setting**, or **Game setting** / catalog row — never the *only* path as a
hard-coded ClaudeCitizen constant. **Defaults and seeds are fine and
encouraged** (schema defaults, New Project scaffold, one-shot migration seeds)
so empty projects boot playable — authors/operators override afterward.
Project = `asteron.project.json`; Scene = **File → Scene Settings…**;
GameSettings / catalog = Server Console.
[Content delivery](../../docs/docs/architecture/content-delivery.md). Client
localStorage graphics prefs ≠ `GameSettings`.

When adding tunables, scene-level options, defaults/seeds, starter grants, or
seedable catalog (factions, curves, …), read the full doc first. Also listed in
`AGENTS.md`.
